Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:48:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1141/1157] perf(serve): build the session-list kanban
 annotation at boot, before the Desktop reconnect burst [daveey]

A cold annotation (nothing served yet for the scope) made every annotate_kanban_activity caller wait on the
single in-flight pass: /api/sessions, /api/profiles/sessions, the sidebar and the one-row
GET /api/sessions/<id>. On example-hub that pass (remote-links projection over the board replicas plus the
board counts) costs ~0.7 s CPU alone and ran 5-10 s inside the restart burst (/api/sessions 9.79 s,
session detail 3.6-4.3 s waiting at _annotation_snapshot). The backend now starts that read on a daemon
thread during the lifespan, like the kanban board prewarm, so the first poll finds the snapshot or joins
the read already under way. Skipped under HERMES_TEST_ISOLATION.
